Q2. There is a biker going on a road trip. The road trip consists of n + 1 points at different altitudes. The biker starts his trip on point 0 with altitude equal 0.
You are given an integer array gain of length n where gain[i] is the net gain in altitude between points i​​​​​​ and i + 1 for all (0 <= i < n). Return the highest altitude of a point.

Sol. 
class Solution {
    public int largestAltitude(int[] gain) {
        int n = gain.length;
        int[] alt = new int[n+1];
        int max = 0 ;
        alt[0] = 0;

        for(int i = 0 ; i < n ; i++){
            alt[i+1] = alt[i] + gain[i];
            if(alt[i+1] > max){
                max = alt[i+1];
            }
        }
        return max;
    }
}

